blueline: SoC and battery temperatures for thermalmonitord (bluethermal=1)

BlueThermal on IOResources makes one HID temperature service (0xFF00, 0x05) per
sensor name in D22AP-Info.plist that the phone can stand for: SDM845 TSENS for the
die sensors (Gold, Silver, L3, GPU, always-on, memory, Wi-Fi, camera, video, modem;
first, mean or highest), the battery gauge (BlueBattery) for TG0B, TG0V and mic1.
thermalmonitord runs its loop only when all non-synthetic sensors are found
("partial sensors: ... mask"). mic1 also sends events every ReportInterval.

